Round-two additions:
native/transport/rdma_gather.cu and src/spark1017/transport.py are generated
from TensorFold's Apache-2.0 transport at the pinned commit below. Registration,
dual-rail proxy, completion notification, abort handling and the original
small-message gather remain upstream. The segmented destination, GPU sequence
tickets, two-segment pipeline and fused HC receive kernel are Spark1017 changes.
native/transport/fused_post.inc preserves the upstream HC arithmetic order.
src/spark1017/postmix.py adapts the Apache-2.0 hc_pre2 side-stream schedule; it reuses
upstream numerical kernels. The prompt dependency split and network integration
are extensions, not a claim to invent HC, speculative decoding or RDMA fusion.
native/persistent and native/chain include generated portions of upstream
experts_grouped.cuh; upstream Apache-2.0 and historical MIT notices are retained in LICENSES/.
compat/ada-drafter.patch guards unsupported programmatic-dependent-launch
instructions on the optional RTX4090 helper. These experiments default off.

native/engram_io.cpp derives from TensorFold engram_io.cpp at
https://github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold/commit/07aa02585f64cfb04c60a96de6554c0d4708ed46
Base file SHA256: e2b0e2833c44c4c108413806bda2abd00342034b1db557e4df37a38082b8a83e
Changes: exact partition residency, bounded row cache, duplicate-read fanout,
configuration interfaces and read counters. Existing Linux AIO and thread-pool
implementation, CUDA kernels, tensor parallel transport, model execution and
DSpark drafting are upstream work, not new work by this project.

native/tiered_store.hpp and src/spark1017 contain the new cache and controller
implementations. prepare_overlay.py introduces hooks into upstream files.
compat/deployment-safety.patch captures pre-existing deployment safety changes;
these are included for reproducing measurements, not claimed as this project's
speed innovation. Preserve the notices in LICENSES/ when redistributing.

Benchmark prompts/clients and the SciCode dataset retain their source licenses.
benchmarks/scicode includes the Apache-2.0 SciCode development JSONL, prompt
template, comparison package and standalone extraction of HDF5 helper functions.
Its README documents the source revisions and adaptations. The numeric HDF5
file is not distributed. CPython edit fixtures preserve the PSF license.
Do not redistribute model weights, credentials, private service configuration
or generated rank caches as part of this project.

benchmarks/canitedit retains a deterministically selected subset of the MIT-licensed
nuprl/CanItEdit dataset and its license. Prompt attribution and protocol changes
are documented alongside its independent HTTP and sandbox harness.

The pinned TensorFold fork and current MiaAI recipe are Apache-2.0. Their
original NOTICE files are included. Historical MIT notices referenced by the
upstream third-party notices are retained for those components; they do not
relicense the newly added DeepSeek family or RDMA transport as MIT.
